  "interpretation": [
    "All three direct runs pass. Two of three adaptive MediaMTX runs pass; the second retains its failed verdict because a 0.212s baseline freeze occurs before network shaping.",
    "All six return to 720p30 and recover the source target. Every format, network-response and resource-lifecycle gate passes. None has steady constrained-network or recovery freezes or steady dropped frames. The first MediaMTX run drops two frames during the initial transition; its total disruption is 1.382652s, including those frames under the unchanged rule. The other five have no dropped frames.",
    "The failed baseline has a 200ms frame-callback gap. Its adjacent frames arrive 28.1ms apart and advance 3000 RTP ticks, while expected presentation advances 216.7ms; the delayed frame reports 1.1ms processing. Sampled loss/NACK/RTX counters do not increase and the JavaScript timer reports at most 17.3ms delay in the affected sample. This localizes the observation to delayed browser presentation but does not establish its cause or prove a healthy host scheduler.",
    "The runner performance-environment gate checks transport-buffer warnings, not host scheduling. Whole-run cgroup resource samples cannot attribute CPU cost to individual source formats. These cases have no pixel-latency probe.",
    "The media image digests are identical between the initial pair at 4cf2b68 and the four repeats at ce008b0. Those source revisions differ only in documentation and retained evidence.",
    "No playback gate was relaxed and failed cases remain failed. The one-second setting remains opt-in experimental; the public three-second default is unchanged pending full qualification."
  ],
